  "before_edn": "{:db/id 17592186184351 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186183947 :question/id #uuid \"70fd3433-e905-5643-8e55-0bdf774d781e\" :question/math-academy-id \"e-14404\" :question/problem \"Calculate  $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\\\, \\\\textrm{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u = e^{2x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\dfrac{\\\\textrm{d}u}{\\\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\\\quad\\\\Longrightarrow\\\\quad\\n\\\\dfrac{1}{2}\\\\, \\\\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\\\, \\\\textrm{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}+1|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}+1)+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x.$\"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid \"ed3b6c3d-b840-50ef-9e6b-584bf14877b3\" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049443 :topic/difficulty 1.2233896690425385 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id 17592186428224 :encompassing/rationale \"Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1361->30. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json.\" :encompassing/topic {:db/id 17592186049195} :encompassing/weight 0.5}] :topic/id #uuid \"f580d418-6860-5b04-b964-2999aa08b42f\" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id 17592186105715} {:db/id 17592186105716} {:db/id 17592186105720}] :topic/math-academy-id 1361 :topic/next [{:db/id 17592186048557} {:db/id 17592186048754}] :topic/title \"Integrating the Reciprocal Function\"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186184451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"29e54fcf-d2f2-5df4-90db-2d54fb195e46\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186247795} {:answer/id #uuid \"431bf13d-976e-5095-9df8-63b0916664a9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186248025} {:answer/id #uuid \"4fa1568a-384f-58a8-924a-2a38ae937084\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186248140} {:answer/id #uuid \"577a0caf-bf7e-59b5-a4ca-f40167c4fa08\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186248218} {:answer/id #uuid \"87d85e70-9986-5c51-90ba-53c36aea0512\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186248638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4fa1568a-384f-58a8-924a-2a38ae937084\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186248140} :answer-field/id #uuid \"792f7b0f-b886-5c74-9417-ec3ce40c477b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186249878}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"2445485f-2474-5b96-9886-76e2b061635a\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-113852\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{3x}+2.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\text{d}u=2{e}^{3x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int {({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\\\cdot 2{e}^{3x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int {u}^{3}\\\\,\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\int {u}^{3}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186184452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"b970921c-d15d-53a0-b5c6-fc46e6dcab7b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}{\\\\ln 3} + C\" :db/id 17592186180890} {:answer/id #uuid \"d778ab08-7f17-5d9d-8fac-d2f1898f19d6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}{6\\\\ln 3} + C\" :db/id 17592186180891} {:answer/id #uuid \"e134739a-8071-5865-951f-b5b40b3c8ea4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}{3\\\\ln 3} + C\" :db/id 17592186180892} {:answer/id #uuid \"e6051283-eee8-5ca7-aef7-508bb9f721c6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}{\\\\ln 3} + C\" :db/id 17592186180893} {:answer/id #uuid \"53948032-e541-5f9a-a89d-710bf093f2e2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}{2\\\\ln 3} + C\" :db/id 17592186180894}] :answer-field/id #uuid \"ffc72a8c-7d71-520d-87f2-59d147ec95f7\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186180889}] :question/id #uuid \"7818d7dd-cee4-50cd-9c8b-99419a2fa97a\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-113876\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int\\\\frac{3^{x + 1}}{\\\\sqrt{3^{x} + 1}}dx.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186234356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"23b3ff8f-fef3-5d4b-8ac7-c7f0be3c20e4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186339438} {:answer/id #uuid \"36b29201-973e-54a1-9076-d11d6f4d33f1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}+C\" :db/id 17592186339618} {:answer/id #uuid \"714604c9-2b37-531a-bb67-a0c67b2a5cb6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186340134} {:answer/id #uuid \"d56615b3-79b5-569f-a38a-6eae7ea1c379\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{2\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186341017} {:answer/id #uuid \"dcc1530c-4d98-5329-89c2-53ade6de9cab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}+C\" :db/id 17592186341089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"714604c9-2b37-531a-bb67-a0c67b2a5cb6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186340134} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9441441f-4088-5ff2-aa37-6b852eabed90\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341641}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"9aadcdf1-9134-541b-ab5d-b526e490dc48\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73670\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u={2}^{z}-9.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}z}={2}^{z}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={2}^{z}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\\\cdot {2}^{z}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186250127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"04d4c17e-b4e9-5c3d-8e37-585ca78e36f0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{{e}^{2x}}+C\" :db/id 17592186247458} {:answer/id #uuid \"5dbb5507-aaa0-5749-a41a-43f26c688149\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186248276} {:answer/id #uuid \"b5da3429-fa5a-5c1e-bc1f-55c28c97d965\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{2{e}^{2x}}+C\" :db/id 17592186249052} {:answer/id #uuid \"b800b44e-6e5f-530d-a74e-e61c336c427d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{{e}^{2x}}+C\" :db/id 17592186249070} {:answer/id #uuid \"c9a200ad-d245-5814-a41d-3e6f3d647290\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186249218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c9a200ad-d245-5814-a41d-3e6f3d647290\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186249218} :answer-field/id #uuid \"1a658127-d29f-5d3c-9088-48b067088416\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186249714}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"e2191fab-edb1-5e72-a762-ef056bc648a3\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-113873\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}-2x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={e}^{2x}-2x.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}-2=2({e}^{2x}-1)\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\text{d}u=({e}^{2x}-1)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}-2x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}-2x}\\\\cdot ({e}^{2x}-1)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}-2x|}{2}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186297410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"398d7153-dd3c-5a82-b5a4-cae2a584156a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5x}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186295595} {:answer/id #uuid \"4ca4abb9-0851-5c3b-9177-0dd90d8d8845\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186295704} {:answer/id #uuid \"7a287bc3-0892-5d93-8218-78604cf894d1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186295934} {:answer/id #uuid \"7ef3b95e-bd1a-57ef-8fe5-5cd8afb14244\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186295954} {:answer/id #uuid \"af23df45-3861-5a0d-ac36-df9c438d8eb0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{5\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186296190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4ca4abb9-0851-5c3b-9177-0dd90d8d8845\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C\" :db/id 17592186295704} :answer-field/id #uuid \"04a5f69b-9de4-5df4-950b-038dd6a88814\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186296647}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"cb025f0b-ba4d-525b-a215-9bdb02362821\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-31478\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{5}^{x}}{{5}^{x}+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={5}^{x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}={5}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={5}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{5}^{x}}{{5}^{x}+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}+1}\\\\cdot {5}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{5}^{x}+1|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that ${5}^{x}+1>0$ for all $x.$\"} {:db/id 17592186297411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"07618f82-80dd-5c73-b8a4-2164bc070f03\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x})}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186295304} {:answer/id #uuid \"7fabc313-b7ec-5fea-8e37-3c5a06d43177\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{{4}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186295957} {:answer/id #uuid \"872590b5-df6d-5e6e-9dc4-79994e14eb92\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{4\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186295994} {:answer/id #uuid \"ac13f248-7d32-5d3e-b31a-bf1601844a70\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186296173} {:answer/id #uuid \"b29969af-ede3-53c4-a306-057c9ce68656\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186296208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ac13f248-7d32-5d3e-b31a-bf1601844a70\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\" :db/id 17592186296173} :answer-field/id #uuid \"7f35bb0c-6a4b-5fe9-b22b-03be76e5104e\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186296892}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"fa16c83a-9f14-57ce-8cd3-45bb3a59d16f\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-31480\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{4}^{x}}{{4}^{x}+2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={4}^{x}+2.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}={4}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={4}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{4}^{x}}{{4}^{x}+2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{4}^{x}+2}\\\\cdot {4}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{4}^{x}+2|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that ${4}^{x}+2>0$ for all $x.$\"} {:db/id 17592186332748 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"027a07ce-3cfe-56e8-be37-2a1cb12f5c96\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{5}}+C\" :db/id 17592186329985} {:answer/id #uuid \"21d26b82-340b-5005-b15b-4c394deda50e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186330239} {:answer/id #uuid \"34f46ff9-bbb8-5507-929a-8bf833e4a41a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186330415} {:answer/id #uuid \"b30e1c0f-e528-5e60-ac58-17f053cef19d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"10\\\\sqrt[3]{({e}^{x}+4)^{2}}+C\" :db/id 17592186331531} {:answer/id #uuid \"c31f2fe7-9fe8-531c-bb86-82e9bb1e9492\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{10}{3}\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186331685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c31f2fe7-9fe8-531c-bb86-82e9bb1e9492\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{10}{3}\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186331685} :answer-field/id #uuid \"18e0a5f1-7890-529c-b7ba-c46e029335b7\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186332236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"2a94e796-17ea-59f0-8634-ea54546ad51c\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-49577\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int 5{e}^{x}\\\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{x}+4.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={e}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int 5{e}^{x}\\\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =5\\\\int \\\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\\\cdot {e}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\int \\\\sqrt{u}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\int {u}^{1/2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\cdot \\\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{10}{3}\\\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{10}{3}\\\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186342057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0c85fd39-fb12-5fd0-84ca-1f9410fd86c2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}+C\" :db/id 17592186339238} {:answer/id #uuid \"35d01e19-8df6-5a98-9a4e-a13ff45e59c6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186339607} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba62682b-6375-50c8-ab0e-ae65ecff8935\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186340799} {:answer/id #uuid \"f040dd33-55b8-577d-b65c-882719ad8257\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}+C\" :db/id 17592186341244} {:answer/id #uuid \"fbec05e7-3328-5ebb-a6b8-92e98b6e67b7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186341354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ba62682b-6375-50c8-ab0e-ae65ecff8935\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C\" :db/id 17592186340799} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9475f005-9702-55df-8eb5-e3d9087d1fde\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341643}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"4d8e2bdb-04c0-5bb8-8174-6e672a971ff9\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73669\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int {2}^{x+1}\\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u={2}^{x}-5.$ Differentiating gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x} & ={2}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={2}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int {2}^{x+1}\\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int 2\\\\cdot {2}^{x}\\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\int \\\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\\\cdot {2}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\int \\\\sqrt{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\int {u}^{1/2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{\\\\left(\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\cdot {u}^{3/2} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186608168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0f888669-2477-534b-93c1-14dd41a1467c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}+C\" :db/id 17592186607822} {:answer/id #uuid \"8a28e55e-aa6e-55ec-9c6f-983a66c3f811\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}+C\" :db/id 17592186607968} {:answer/id #uuid \"a422661a-62b6-548f-99fb-b5e248bf15ef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}}+C\" :db/id 17592186607999} {:answer/id #uuid \"dd7625c3-f004-5df2-addc-77e2835786c9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+2}+C\" :db/id 17592186608048} {:answer/id #uuid \"ef774d49-b81e-572f-9499-ca77b619a297\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}+C\" :db/id 17592186608069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0f888669-2477-534b-93c1-14dd41a1467c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}+C\" :db/id 17592186607822} :answer-field/id #uuid \"060253c5-cf85-5b59-9850-bd847d9b4cdb\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186608091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"14a57d7f-2f51-563e-9400-c8274f6aaa38\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-49574\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{e}^{z}}{\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{z}+1.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}z}={e}^{z}\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={e}^{z}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{e}^{z}}{\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}}\\\\cdot {e}^{z}\\\\,\\\\text{d}z \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\sqrt{{e}^{z}+1}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186608178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"34c67ac0-41e8-5678-8336-d0107e58afba\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\" :db/id 17592186607865} {:answer/id #uuid \"4d4864b2-2c2f-57f4-956b-9433730346bd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\" :db/id 17592186607904} {:answer/id #uuid \"70f388a5-6722-5425-b634-fd9fcace933e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{6\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\" :db/id 17592186607939} {:answer/id #uuid \"7e2d864c-a850-55c1-893b-e69551329f80\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-6\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|+C\" :db/id 17592186607958} {:answer/id #uuid \"8f824d94-ffac-51cd-ade0-eac66ce2397f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{6\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\" :db/id 17592186607971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"34c67ac0-41e8-5678-8336-d0107e58afba\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\" :db/id 17592186607865} :answer-field/id #uuid \"be0455fc-1523-58f5-9e10-d164fbc5cf2a\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186608146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"35f0c1cb-49ca-5544-8236-0e4cefc5c8cd\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-113875\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{6}^{x}}{2-{6}^{x}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u=2-{6}^{x}.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=-{6}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\\\,⟹\\\\,-\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={6}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{6}^{x}}{2-{6}^{x}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{2-{6}^{x}}\\\\cdot {6}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\left(-\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\\\right)\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-{6}^{x}|}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186627685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0ab0391c-aba7-5b4b-b924-823a0ecf8ef0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{{2}^{2-3{x}^{2}}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627112} {:answer/id #uuid \"282c73af-4464-5ea1-be06-b83bdc954507\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{{2}^{1-3{x}^{3}}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627163} {:answer/id #uuid \"64b77f22-9abf-56fe-8cb2-efe9fed08e09\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3\\\\cdot {2}^{3-3{x}^{3}}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627264} {:answer/id #uuid \"7516a0db-3848-55de-b5a0-79b72e92b866\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{{2}^{1-3{x}^{3}}}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627290} {:answer/id #uuid \"bef4977f-efe8-5b57-8f0e-155b8d88345f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{{2}^{3-3{x}^{3}}}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"bef4977f-efe8-5b57-8f0e-155b8d88345f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{{2}^{3-3{x}^{3}}}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\" :db/id 17592186627409} :answer-field/id #uuid \"84fca298-420b-5070-8302-520084591405\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186627601}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"45b28540-4478-5f51-a0e6-dbeb90f3ba88\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73666\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int 6{x}^{2}\\\\,{2}^{2-3{x}^{3}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's introduce the new variable $u=2-3{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=-9{x}^{2}\\\\,⟹\\\\,-\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int 6{x}^{2}\\\\,{2}^{2-3{x}^{3}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =6\\\\int {2}^{2-3{x}^{3}}\\\\,\\\\cdot {x}^{2}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =6\\\\int {2}^{u}\\\\cdot \\\\left(-\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\right)\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\int {2}^{u}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{{2}^{u}}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{{2}^{1}\\\\cdot {2}^{2-3{x}^{3}}}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\\\\\  & =-\\\\frac{{2}^{3-3{x}^{3}}}{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186664062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"70a9e400-9f93-57ab-9a14-7ffb9d25e219\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x+1}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663694} {:answer/id #uuid \"ac6d1d4d-fceb-50d0-b5e6-abfc0eb65dde\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663796} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba253305-8757-572e-8b4a-4c6a6d188d9d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x}+1)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663821} {:answer/id #uuid \"d9d02898-740e-54de-af62-005f64fa7dd5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x-1}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663879} {:answer/id #uuid \"e1d58cd5-60ac-5ca2-8082-2c6c2008174d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ac6d1d4d-fceb-50d0-b5e6-abfc0eb65dde\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\" :db/id 17592186663796} :answer-field/id #uuid \"dbfdfb0e-1c45-5415-8a60-6b10719a32f2\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186664017}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"50d988aa-30cb-58ec-89a4-3a5bc9d0a71a\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-113872\" :question/problem \"Calculate the integral $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{{3}^{x+1}}{{3}^{x}+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={3}^{x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u={3}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{{3}^{x+1}}{{3}^{x}+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}+1}\\\\cdot {3}^{x+1}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}+1}\\\\cdot 3\\\\cdot {3}^{x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{u}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\\\,\\\\text{d}u \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{3}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{3\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x}+1)}{\\\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that ${3}^{x}+1>0$ for all $x.$\"}] :knowledge-point/title \"More Complex Cases\"}",
  "records": [
    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186184351,
        "id": "ed3b6c3d-b840-50ef-9e6b-584bf14877b3",
        "title": "More Complex Cases"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "5196a682-3b3b-548b-8bcb-d71c48d9fec1",
        ":question/problem": "Use the substitution $u=2^{x} + 2$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\cdot 2^{x} \\left(2^{x} + 2\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2^{x} + 2$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2^{x} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork where $2^{x} + 2>0$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\cdot 2^{x} \\left(2^{x} + 2\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\left(\\int u^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\left(\\int u^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
