      "question": {
        ":question/id": "0156d36e-072e-5215-9c38-b10ce4b47e6d",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 \\cdot 3^{x} \\sqrt{3^{x} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{2 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+C$.\n\nWork where $3^{x} + 4>0$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3^{x} + 4$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork where $3^{x} + 4>0$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\cdot 3^{x} \\sqrt{3^{x} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{4}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\frac{2 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(3^{x} + 4\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "a79080ff-3a68-56f4-bd9c-22a0870f1b37",
